## Deadly Mantis

Deadly mantises are mantis-like insects the size of a person that hunt in the depths of the [[Verdant Expanse]]. One can pass for a stand of leaves on a tree until it moves. They have green bodies, a wing shaped like leaves, and an extended insect's head, and they skitter quickly over the ground. They can hear, and a loud noise staggers them.

They hunt by leaping from trees and seizing their prey, and they work in packs. Their blood is greenish-blue, and a hard enough blow can chop one's thorax in two.

## Mioktan

Mioktans are centipede-things fifteen feet long, and they fight from a distance, flinging whatever is at hand. One can grow a club of bone out of an arm.

Two of them guarded the drug works at 414 Anchor Street in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Deosil|Deosil]] for [[People/Sbrtlby Jotes|Sbrtlby Jotes]], alongside three [[Bestiary/Fiends|pusks]]. Both are dead.

## Swarm Child

Swarms of two-foot-tall insectoid creatures live in the vents of [[Geography/Istria/Iomenei/index|Iomenei]]. Each has a chitinous body in purplish orange, a hard-looking head and nasty fangs, and three claws on each hand, and they scrabble out of the vents in numbers. They rush over anyone close and bite with their mandibles, and they spit a corrosive spittle at those who keep their distance. As more of a swarm is killed, the rest grow less coordinated.

They have claimed a forsaken sector of the [[Geography/Istria/Iomenei/Undercroft|Undercroft]] as their own. Their kind were bred by the Hivemother, a different and larger sort of bug, which is now dead.

## The Hivemother

The Hivemother was an insectoid creature some eighty feet long, coiled around the central pillar of a cathedral room in the forsaken sector of [[Geography/Istria/Iomenei/index|Iomenei]]. It bred the swarm children, emitting them as it was watched, and a horn grew from its mouth. Its brood claimed the room around it. It was a different kind of bug from the swarm children.

It is dead, killed by [[People/Barlow Crane|Barlow Crane]], [[People/Grant FireEye|Grant FireEye]], [[People/Gage|Gage]] and [[Org/Velvet Mark/People/Archie|Archie]]. Every other insect in the room collapsed where it stood when it was split in two. The saboteur [[People/Gerhard|Gerhard]] was not in its room, and more of the insects may have taken root elsewhere in the city.

## Zabub

Zabubs are the library's workers: half a beetle and half a baby. An insect's shell, legs and mandibles are joined to a small human torso whose arms hang limp. They come out of a pool of black ink and fade back into it. A zabub gets about by pushing itself along with its beetle half, holding itself just off the floor on its wings while its arms drag behind. They carry books in their mandibles and fetch one when a reader asks.

## Scythe-Armed Spider

Scythe-armed spiders are large spiders, blue and black, each bigger than a person. Six of their legs are ordinary spider legs; the front pair is shaped like scythe blades, held up before them as they move. They gather in numbers, and they live in curtains of silk that hang from a ceiling in strands like ropes rather than in a woven web, crossing the strands as easily as a floor. Balls of silk the size of a cartwheel hang among them, holding their eggs. They spit webbing at whatever catches their eye.

A nest of them has taken over a disused stretch of the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]]'s lower decks, where their silk has gummed some of the linkages that drive the strider's legs.

## Apothecary Bug

Apothecary bugs are small spiders that carry a body full of poisons. One leaps onto a person and stings. Its venom leaves the body weak and unsteady, and the sloughing toxin it carries works the muscles loose from the bones. Killed, the bug bursts and spatters the poisons it still held across the floor.

## Hiveling

Hivelings are small spiders that crawl through the webs and around the works of the fane deep in the lower hull of the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]]. They come from the four vats and from the spherical device at the middle of the chamber, and they bite. Each one is small, and they are dangerous as a swarm.
